  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Mine Site Validation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Democratic Republic of the Congo):  .The activity addresses illicit markets for conflict minerals associated with many corrupt practices in the provinces of North and South Kivu, including financing armed groups, money laundering, elite capture of resources, illegal taxation, among other areas. By reinforcing government systems that exist in the law, but have never been put into practice, USAID strengthens a critical governance process called mine site qualification and validation, which ensures mine sites meet standards and national and international criteria. This activity promotes additional transparency and accountability by empowering local actors-particularly civil society, communities and provincial and municipal authorities-to implement continuous and rigorous monitoring of minerals. As an alternative to prior methods of validation that relied on infrequent visits from authorities, USAID&apos;s current approach decreases the risk of corruption by bolstering training and more frequent involvement from local actors, particularly civil society groups. The project helps to assemble local monitoring committees to facilitate the initial qualification of mine sites as well as monitor sites&apos; ongoing adherence to national regulations. Through ongoing security analysis and monitoring of mine sites, the project increases the capacity of staff from the DRC&apos;s Ministry of Mines and strengthens artisanal and small-scale mining cooperatives to address issues like child labor. Through associations of women, FY 2021 funds will raise awareness among local groups of women involved with artisanal mining about the protections provided under existing laws. ..This activity contributes to the Integrated Country Strategy and Country Development Cooperation Strategy via Development Objective 1 &quot;Responsiveness of Public Institutions to Citizens&apos; Needs Improved&quot;..</narrative>
  </description>
